Required --url / MINYMATON_URL / url;
Explicit --token-env / token_env fails closed (exit 1);
never reads client harness JSON or argv secrets

div.br:
2025 MCP: LocalSessionManager;
2026-07-28: sessionless requests;
instructions reflect exposed tools per route;
request cancellation / socket disconnect
cancels receive and drops parked WaitGuard

ACK only after handling;
publish(ack) or receive(max_events: 0, ack)
preserves parked receive ownership;
ACK-only receive omits wait + max_bytes;
any receiving call supersedes prior waiter

div.div:
Compile-Time Policy Enforcement (tools/compiler-lints — rustc HIR driver)
rejects lint suppression attributes and internal timed waits / readiness polling;
normal build, Clippy and CI paths cover workspace library, binary and integration test targets

Queue Coordinator (queue.rs :: Queue · Queue::open / with_backend)
Typed serde validation: required fields + valid action/field combinations (api.rs);
parks receive(wait: true) on Signals outside QueueStore writer lock;
ACK-only publish(ack) / receive(max_events: 0, ack) takes no receive ownership;
receiving calls (including wait: false) supersede the prior owner

CSPRNG Identifiers & Subscription Lifecycle (ids.rs, store.rs)
128-bit random hex IDs (sub_…, msg_…, bat_…); atomic agent-N smallest-free label claim;
start_at: "latest" | "earliest" cursor initialization; action: "delete" cascade freeing retired labels

div.br:
Native Rust minymaton-wait or Python 3 minymaton-wait.py;
sessionless MCP 2026-07-28 headers + _meta;
receive(wait: true), optional handled-batch ACK;
explicit --url / MINYMATON_URL / --config; no initialize

Signals commit / owner watch channels; outside QueueStore lock;
WaitGuard enters process-local waiting observation;
publish(ack) / receive(max_events: 0, ack)
preserves parked owner (omit wait + max_bytes)

Check subscription exists + owner_generation in same tx;
only current owner records delivery attempt;
return complete JSON-RPC response (JSON or SSE);
helper exits 0 with unacknowledged batch on stdout

Native task watcher wakes idle agent; MCP alone cannot;
handle events, deduplicate by batch_id, then ACK;
re-parking when idle remains agent-owned;
at-least-once delivery, not exactly-once handling

Request socket closes or MCP cancellation fires;
context.ct.cancelled() drops parked receive;
guard drop updates active-count watch + waiting;
hard kill needs no helper finally / HTTP cleanup

3 superseded; 4 batch gone; 5 subscription missing;
6 bounds; 7 HTTP / EOF; 1 config / protocol / domain;
130 Ctrl+C; JSON stderr (2 argument usage instead);
resolve cause / ownership; avoid waiter takeover livelock

No sleeps, polling, retry timers or automatic re-arm;
foreground MCP receives remain client-timeout-bound;
half-open TCP without FIN/RST may block indefinitely;
waiting does not prove a remote client is alive
